{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/961953-new-york-city-goblin-market","id":961953,"title":"New York City Goblin Market","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-01T16:11:28-07:00","id":961953,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> New York City Goblin Market","content":"\u200bSo I'm running a Mage the awakening game and my PC's are heading to the goblin market next session. They are after a mage that escaped from the guardians of the veil. They can't track him and think he might have sold his name at the goblin market. (Which he did). They managed to track down the information how to enter it, and have not had any contact with any changelings or their ilk yet.<br /> <br /> I got my roommate to read over my market I came up with and he though I should post it on the forums so others could have a look, use it, or what have you. I got inspiration for many sources when coming out with my vendors, and hope someone else can get some good out of it.<br /> <br /> Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u><b>New York Goblin Market</b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Location:</b> Central park</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Time:</b> Gates can be accessed on Wednesday, Between sundown and sun up.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Gate</b>: <b>Cedar Hill Bridge </b>(Bottom gate)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Key:</b> Must draw a door in chalk under the bridge, and knock 2 times, then 3 very fast, run the 4 fingers of your hand down one edge of the chalk erasing it, and lose some change. (Door will form along the chalk outline, chalk shakes off when it closes)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Other side: Brick wall of surreal graffiti. There is some black ivy with red diamond shaped leaves overlapping it forming a door shape. There is a dark red and green flower with white dots and red thorns that resembles an African Daisy growing in the cracks inside the door shape. It looks like a handle. (Flower moves and snaps at people trying to grab it)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Gate: Bethesda Fountain</b> (Middle gate)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Key: Must take a breath underwater and start drowning, find a penny thrown in the fountain and swallow it.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Other side: There is a fountain that resembles a group girls made out of stone wearing dresses in the style of the 1800's. They look like they are dancing around the center, but are not moving. (Usually) The center has a pile of skeletons crawling over each other trying to reach a golden gem encrusted chalice in the middle. The skeletons look to be real, and covered in posies that look like human skin with a red spotted rash. There is water pouring out of the skeletons mouths. There is a circular rusted metal trap door in the water with a large metal ring and chain in the middle. Pulling the chain open triangle flaps inside and in the shape of the circle. After the circle is open, the chain pulls you through the portal to the other side. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Gate</b>: <b>Hutt in Shakespeares</b> Garden (Top gate)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Key: There is a old wooden door that the key has gone missing to. You Can use a key the you own but don't know what it belongs to to open the door, after destroying something you father owns. (If deceased, something he considered his when alive)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Other side: There is a giants head with one large right arm stitched to it's forehead. There are a dozen or so spikes dug into it flesh and chaining it to the floor and walls. It looks to be in it's 50 or so, and is has a ring of thinning red hair around the back of its head. It has thick bushy eyebrows and stubbly facial hair growth, like a week of growth. It's a little red in the face, and sweaty, as it looks uncomfortable. You have to let it put you in it's mouth and you come back out into the real world. [Sounds like Louis C K. \u201c <i>Hey. Hey you. I want to talk to you. I want to talk to you about getting inside my mouth. I think you want to get in here. HEY YOU! I'm talking to you. You don't have to make a big deal out of it.</i> <span style=\"color:#3a3a3a\"><i>\u2014Anybody wanna get in my mouth? I'm a big mo\u2014hungry monster\u2014I'm a big hungry monster here! I would really appreciate it, if someone\u2014you, ma'am, you ma'am, how would you like to get in my\u2014</i></span>] </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">You come across a long alley with strange creatures walking around perusing the various shops and stalls. The walls are mainly red brick, and you can see large trees, and huge thorny veins over the walls. There are glass lanterns with metal frames along the wall at various locations providing light. The sky overhead is overcast, with a dark greenish ting. The walls are covered in graffiti and writing, posters, and, signs, and alien ivy plants and moss. They tend to move and change around when your not looking. The majority of the stands are wooden with stripped or solid colored tarpaulin roofs. They resemble an old European farmers market. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There are also large hobgoblins patrolling around looking for trouble. [Thumpers: Over 7 feet tall, shades of green and yellows in color, big thick fingers, noises, ears. They have fierce underbites with thick teeth shaped like bullets. They look unintelligent, [Most have 1 int, but high notice rolls] and dangerous. They are wearing black slacks, long sleeve white shirt which are rolled up, black suspenders, and no shoes. All of them are carrying a long man catcher slung over one shoulder with a strap, and knobby club.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Can make a notice roll to spot various red eyed ravens perched high in the market, watching over things. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Mr. Bigs, Galeaebub #1</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Hob that started it all. Set up a permanent market over 150 years ago. He Stands at 3'10, and has dark green skin the texture of a frog. He has a large nose and ears. He has angular cheeks and a pointed chin. His has a short brow. He has gold plated round pointed teeth. His eyes are sunken and yellow. He is wearing black pinstripe pants with a gold long sleeve button shirt. He has dark red double breasted vest on over it and a black western style tie. He had black armbands around upper forearm and there is a gold pocket watch in his pocket, and a black handkerchief in another. He is wearing alligator shoes. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">RP: Very efficient, cold, logical, calculating, very matter of fact, no riddles, wants things to run smoothly, keeps order over everything else [even profit, which is second], money is his ally, and business is business, don't hold a grudge, can forgive if beneficial, brutal to those who breaks his rules, don't kill often, prefers to maim troublemakers. (Gotta teach them a lesson) Resides in a Wooden office with many large mirrors instead of windows. [<span style=\"color:#000000\">One-way mirrors] </span>Office suspend over the heart of the market. Connects by wooden stairs, rope bridges, and ladders</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Always travels with 2 oversize Hobs named Knuckles and Bruno.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Market Law</b></span></span><br /> \u2022 <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">No Violence. </span></span><br /> \u2022 <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">You Get What\u2019s Advertised.</span></span><br /> \u2022 <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Honor Your Deals.</span></span><br /> \u2022 <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">No Refunds. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Almost all stalls keep a basket with a few goblin fruits in it, and a few Oddments or Gewgaws for bargaining. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Haggling</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dice Pool: Manipulation + Persuasion + equipment versus Manipulation + Persuasion + equipment</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Action: Extended and contested (3-10+ successes required; each roll represents a couple of rounds or minutes of debate)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Both Parties roll to meet the difficulty. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Results: </b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If the winner has only a simple majority of successes, he must concede to half of the competitors demands</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If the winner has double the competitors successes, the winner must concede to a quarter of the competitors demands.</span></span></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If the winner has three times the competitors successes, no concessions are required.</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Suggested Equipment:</b> Access to the <i>Guide to the Goblin Market</i> (+1), pertinent background information on the market vendor (+1), Goblin market stall (+2), resources to bribe (+3), information to blackmail the opposition (+1 to +5), impressive clothing (+1),</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Possible Penalties:</b> Lack of market etiquette (-1), Offending a merchant (-1 to -3), language barriers (-2 to -5),<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dealer: Grek #2</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stand: 3 Sides, against wall, he sits in the middle, solid wood frame border roof with tarpaulin center. Baskets of odd fruits places around stand with some hanging from the roof. There are several barrels behind the stand and some sacks. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A gruff little creature sits on a high stool smoking a pipe. Its only 4 feet tall, and has a big noes and ears. Its eyes are beady like a rat and its skin is the color of dyed mustard, and textured like a frog. It has a pair of glasses perched on its noes, and it wearing gray 1950's business suit.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">wares: Goblin Fruits, some esoteric times,</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">RP Notes: Dislikes Sean. Gruff, and bitter. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dealer: Bearagulg (Bear.ah.gull.ed) #3</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stand: No stand</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stands at over 30 feet in height (32.8 feet), This creature resembles a Ent from fantasy. It has 2 &quot;legs&quot;, arms, and a face in the bark of it's wood. It's resembles a red oak, with bright ref and orange leaves. There appears to be hundreds of branches of different trees grafted to it at different points.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">RP: Talks slow, hymn, hymn, let me see, hard to upset, likes jokes, gives discounts for people talking a good joke or story</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wares: Goblin Fruits, some knick-knacks and such from time to times.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dealer: The Masked Madam (She has no name of her own) #4</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stand: 3 Sides against a wall. Wooden. Has a silver tarpaulin roof that occasionally sprinkles sparkling warm light. (Like a sparkler). There is a tall shelf of items behind her, and some small ones on display around the sides of the stand. There is a large eye with bat wings hanging upside down by tiny clawed feet (Has eyelids and some furry mass around the eye) in a metal cage. The cage is hanging from black metal poll near the right side inside the stand. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The figure standing before you is tall, a little over 6 foot (6'1). Its wearing deep blue robes with gold trim. Its has a white porcelain mask for a face. Head rapped in a gold head scarf.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">RP: Talks is a wispy low voice, but not whispering. No emotion. Moves around likes shes floating.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wares: tokens, some esoteric items, some goblin fruits </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">(Kelta berries, (provided the 9 again rule on the next roll for a int based skills) </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dealer: Jack (Changeling) [Second Born] #5</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stand: 3 Sides against the wall. Red and white stripped tarpaulin. Door on wall with a lock. 3 Shelves behind stand with many trinkets and items on them. No items in front. There is a creature sitting behind a small desk tinkering with some object. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Standing at 5'9, He has a thin but athletic build. He has candles instead of eyes, and a wide mouth stitched at the ends. His head looks like its covered in a burlap cloth, and he had short black hair. There is a rope around his neck, and he usually wears a black hoodie and blue jeans. Its hard to put an age to him, he sounds like an adult. (Hes 24, he was taken when he was 12, and got out when he was 18.)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">RP notes: Talks fairly nonchalant, Likes scaring adults, and hates dogs. Hes the master token craftsman for the court. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wares: Tokens, makes them</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dealer: Puss and Putter #6</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stand: 2 sides against wall, triangle design. Tarpaulin Is half dark blue, half emerald green. There are 2 anthropomorphic cats on the counter top. One is lying on (Puss) a pile of plastic bags in a cardboard box used to hold bottled water and the other is sitting on book and some paper with its legs hanging over the side. (Putter) [All items are below and behind the counter,] </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">These twins resemble a 3 foot tall cats twisted into a humanoid form. They are both black with amber eyes. Puss is dresses like puss in boots, while putter is wearing a simple yellow dress with white frills. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">RP: Puss acts like puss in boots, Putter acts like a southern bell</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wares: Puss is a trainer of occult, melee, and barters in information. Putter can teach goblin contracts [Also sells catnip on the side, make you irresistible to the ladies, but only cats of course]. They also have a few tokens</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dealer: William #7</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stand: Looks like a kids lemonade stand, with a sign over head that looks like random swirls of colors. There is a creature perched on a tall wooden stool sneering at people.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">He stands at 5'10, and is usually hunched over. His naked body is covered in thick dark brown hair, and his skull is longer than a man. He has feral eyes, and his face has bestial features. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">RP notes: hes a creep, sneaky, lying, rubs hands together when excited and hops</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wares: Sells subterfuge, larceny, and stealth. (also sells small human slaves on the down low, won't offer to most humans and changeling as they tend to disprove.)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dealer: The Social Monster (James P. &quot;Sulley&quot; Sullivan) #8</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stand: Its off to the side, with a small round wood table with 3 red leather chairs around it. There is a end table with a lamp on it near its chair, and a small bookshelf.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">It stands at 6'6 and is covered in light blue fur. It has a large wide build like a grizzly bear. It has short legs ending in claws, and large long arms also ending in claws. It has yellow eyes and a large black noise that looks like a cats. It has a mild snout, and large black horns like a water buffalo. It's wearing a pair of narrow reading glasses. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">RP: Very polite, intelligent, smokes a pipe, has at lest 4 in all social attributes and many specialties. He is charismatic but scared of children and germs. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wares: Sells social merits and skill. Can magically infuse, or teach the old fashion way. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dealer: The Smiling Man #9</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stand: Standing next to a wall with a long wooden trap door on the ground. There is a unpainted wooden board on the wall with Polaroids of people, creatures, and animals stuck to it with thumb tacks. The trap door reveals a wooden staircase heading down. Sound can be hear coming for it when the door is open. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Looks to be a man, 7 feet tall with yellow skin. He looks to be 50's, with a ring of black hair around the back of his head. He's wearing solid black round glasses and is very wrinkly, unnaturally so. He has a long neck, and a rounder head than he should. Wearing a black tux jacket with coat tails. His clothing looks to be mad of wax.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">RP: Always smiling, wants to make a deal, bows and likes to shake hands. Will hand out small yellow slim envelopes to customers. Has a number written on a piece of torn paper. [A human contact in the real world] </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wares: Slaves [Hob goblins, some human, intelligent animals, monsters like an owl bear. All slaves are terrified of him]</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dealer: Harold Zidler (Zidlers) #10</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stand: Looks like a small red and yellow stripped circus tent. Door is 6'6 ft high and 2'8 ft wide. Tent isn't much bigger than that. There is a red curtain acting as a door. The inside is far bigger, about the size of a ball room. Inside is a large dance floor with a stage with large red curtains. The floor along the sides of the dance floor is raised and behind a rail and there are round tables and chair placed their. There is a second floor with a rail around it, and some booths like that at a theater. Besides the 2 staircases on the side of the room going to the second floor, there are thick curtains along the side hiding small curved rooms with small stages and crescent shaped seats for private dances.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">When you enter, you see dozens of male creatures dancing with female ones. There is a large anthropomorphic creature stirring up a commotion, keeping the crowd lively. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">A Kingdom of nightmarish pleasure. There are many beautiful and twisted creatures ready to fulfill your hearts desire. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The creature It stands at 6'8, and appears to be a giant bipedal red crocodile with black stripes. wearing a green ring master outfit with black trim. It has a cane a top hat. He has a white shirt and white bow tie on with a gold vest, black pants, but no shoes. Oddly, he has is wearing a human mask, suspended at the end of his snout, with a long string holding the mask to it's head like a cheep Halloween mask. The mask resembles Herold Zidler from the 2001 Moulin Rouge! Movie. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">RP: Very theatrical, Can sing and dance well. \u201cJust scratch the little niggle, have a little wiggle. Got some dark desire, love to play with fire, why not let it rip, live a little bit. Outside things may be tragic, but in here we feel it's magic, yeah whoa!\u201d Calls his ladies My little....insert playful word. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wares: He sell intelligent animals, breeds them, also runs a Burlesque house. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dealer: Darwin Bark #11</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stand: 3 Sides with 2 flip up parts on the counter to let people back. There is no back wall, instead heading into what appears to be a tailor shop with many rolls of fabrics, and a exotic sowing machine. Many draws, manikin, cloths of display. There is a large Drider, about twice the size of a person behind working on a dress made of sunset. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Furry white with some black. Drider. Upper torso of a man, wearing a expensive looking long sleeve black shirt made of storm clouds (Sleeves rolled up), and a blue and white tie made of lightening. and a white vest made of snow with a black pocket watch. Looks to be in his late 50's with styled white hair. Has a pair of glasses.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">RP: Love his job, loves to make other looks good, one of the more &quot;fair&quot;, other vendors think hes weird, usually throws in a little extra. </span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Is asexual... He Doesn't want to be eaten.</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> think of Barneys tailor, played by actor Tim Gunn.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wares: Hedge spun tailor. Can sew anything out of anything. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dealer: Her Majesty (True Fae) #12</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stand: You hear the buzzing before you approach. You come across a gigantic (over 20 ft high) bee hive against a brick 